          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "The order of acidic strength of boron trihalides",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "oG98Q",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Izk7z",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "uHxd0",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "CsNXt",
              "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>The strength of acidic character of boron trihalides depends upon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>p&#960;</mi></math> back bonding.</p><p>In boron trihalides, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>p&#960;</mi></math> -back bonding occurs due to empty orbital of boron and filled orbitals of halogens.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/bf2f12fc-7efd-4bd8-b002-c137c0c9320c-image.png\" style=\"width: 398px; height: 255px;\" /></p><p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>p&#960;</mi></math> back bonding is shown maximum by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, as the size of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> are small and comparatively same. Due to this effect tendency of accepting lone-pair of electrons of boron decreases as size of halogen increases. The order of size of halogens are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>. Thus, acidic nature is in order</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BBr</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>BI</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
