              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "More the oxidation state of the central atom (metal) more is its acidity. Hence $\\mathrm{SeO}_{2}(\\mathrm{O} . \\mathrm{S} .$ of $\\mathrm{Se}=+4)$ is acidic. Further for a given O.S., the basic character of the oxides increases with the increasing size of the central atom. Thus $\\mathrm{Al}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{Sb}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$ are amphoteric and $\\mathrm{Bi}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$ is basic.",
            "image": null
